pagpapatupad ng mga environmental laws at regulations?\",\"choices\":[\"Pabilisin ang pag-unlad ng industriya\",\"Protektahan ang kalikasan at kalusugan ng publiko\",\"Patawan ng buwis ang mga negosyo\",\"Hikayatin ang paggamit ng plastic\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Ano ang tawag sa pagkawala ng sari-saring uri ng mga halaman at hayop?\",\"choices\":[\"Habitat loss\",\"Biodiversity loss\",\"Climate change\",\"Pollution\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Alin sa mga sumusunod ang isang pang-ekonomiyang solusyon sa mga isyung pangkapaligiran?\",\"choices\":[\"Pagbabawal sa lahat ng industriya\",\"Pagbibigay ng insentibo sa mga kumpanyang gumagamit ng malinis na teknolohiya\",\"Pagpapalaki ng gastusin sa militar\",\"Pagsasanay sa mga sundalo\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Ano ang epekto ng pagkakalbo ng mga bundok sa suplay ng tubig?\",\"choices\":[\"Pagdami ng tubig-ilog\",\"Pagbaba ng tubig-ilog at pagtaas ng panganib ng landslide\",\"Paglinis ng tubig-ilog\",\"Pagtaas ng presyo ng tubig\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Alin sa mga sumusunod ang halimbawa ng paggamit ng \'reduce\' sa 3Rs (Reduce, Reuse, Recycle)?\",\"choices\":[\"Pagbili ng maraming bagong gamit\",\"Paggamit muli ng mga lumang lalagyan\",\"Pagbawas sa pagkonsumo ng mga bagay na hindi kailangan\",\"Paghahandog ng mga basura sa recycling center\"],\"correct_index\":2,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Ano ang koneksyon sa pagitan ng kahirapan at isyung pangkapaligiran?\",\"choices\":[\"Ang mga mahihirap ay hindi apektado ng pagkasira ng kapaligiran.\",\"Ang mga mahihirap ay kadalasang mas apektado ng pagkasira ng kapaligiran dahil sa kanilang limitadong kakayahang umangkop at mas nakadepende sila sa likas na yaman.\",\"Ang kahirapan ang sanhi ng pagiging malinis ng kapaligiran.\",\"Walang kaugnayan ang kahirapan sa isyung pangkapaligiran.\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1}]',20,'pdf','8832bc00732d851bab0b64a86c0c9909.pdf','araling_panlipunan_10_quiz_mga_isyung_pangkapaligiran_at_pan.pdf','application/pdf',115191,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Generated','2026-09-20 08:14:59','2026-09-20 08:14:59',NULL,NULL),(3,20,'MAPEH7',NULL,'quiz','MAPEH 7: Philippine Folk Songs Quiz','for Philippine folk songs','# MAPEH 7: Philippine Folk Songs Quiz\n\nInstructions: Read each question carefully and choose the best answer.\n\n1. What is the primary characteristic of most Philippine folk songs?\nA. They are often about love and courtship.\nB. They are usually religious in nature.\nC. They often tell stories of daily life, history, or cultural practices.\nD. They are exclusively sung in Spanish.\n\n2. Which of the following is a popular example of a children\'s folk song from the Philippines?\nA. \"Noche Buena\"\nB. \"Bahay Kubo\"\nC. \"Leron Leron Sinta\"\nD. \"Magtanim Ay Di Biro\"\n\n3. \"Leron Leron Sinta\" is a folk song that describes the hardships of:\nA. Farmers harvesting rice.\nB. A person looking for a guava.\nC. Fishermen at sea.\nD. Children playing a game.\n\n4. \"Magtanim Ay Di Biro\" is a folk song that highlights the challenges and nature of work for:\nA. Weavers of traditional cloth.\nB. Farmers planting rice.\nC. Musicians performing in fiestas.\nD. Sailors navigating the seas.\n\n5. Folk songs in the Philippines often use simple melodies and are passed down through generations. This is an example of:\nA. Classical music notation.\nB. Oral tradition.\nC. Formal musical training.\nD. Electronic music composition.\n\n6. Many Philippine folk songs have lyrics that reflect the local environment and daily activities. Which song best exemplifies this?\nA. \"Dandansoy\"\nB. \"Paruparong Bukid\"\nC. \"Tong, Tong, Tong Pakitong-kitong\"\nD. \"Sarung Banggi\"\n\n7. \"Dandansoy\" is a folk song that originated from which region of the Philippines?\nA. Luzon\nB. Visayas\nC. Mindanao\nD. Palawan\n\n8. The song \"Sarung Banggi\" is known for its:\nA. Fast tempo and complex rhythm.\nB. Melancholy tune about lost love.\nC. Simple, sweet melody and lyrics about the night.\nD. Depiction of a lively fiesta.\n\n9. What is the significance of folk songs in preserving Philippine culture?\nA. They promote foreign music genres.\nB. They are solely for entertainment purposes.\nC. They carry stories, values, and traditions of the Filipino people.\nD. They are only taught in music schools.\n\n10. The song \"Bahay Kubo\" describes a house made of simple, local materials and the food grown around it. This reflects:\nA. Modern architecture in cities.\nB. The abundance of natural resources and simple living in the countryside.\nC. The influence of foreign cultures on Filipino homes.\nD. The challenges of urban living.','# MAPEH 7: Philippine Folk Songs Quiz - Answer Key\n\n1. C. They often tell stories of daily life, history, or cultural practices.\n   *Explanation: Philippine folk songs are rich in narrative, often reflecting the daily lives, beliefs, and history of the communities they come from.\n2. C. \"Leron Leron Sinta\"\n   *Explanation: While \"Magtanim Ay Di Biro\" is also a well-known folk song, \"Leron Leron Sinta\" is a classic example often sung by children and adults alike, with a story about a person trying to pick fruit.\n3. B. A person looking for a guava.\n   *Explanation: The lyrics of \"Leron Leron Sinta\" tell the story of a person who tries to pick a ripe guava but fails.\n4. B. Farmers planting rice.\n   *Explanation: \"Magtanim Ay Di Biro\" vividly describes the tiring labor involved in rice farming.\n5. B. Oral tradition.\n   *Explanation: Folk songs are typically learned and passed down from one generation to the next through listening and singing, rather than formal written scores.\n6. C. \"Tong, Tong, Tong Pakitong-kitong\"\n   *Explanation: This song humorously describes a crab that is caught and cooked, reflecting everyday experiences and observations.\n7. B. Visayas\n   *Explanation: \"Dandansoy\" is a popular folk song originating from the Visayas region.\n8. C. Simple, sweet melody and lyrics about the night.\n   *Explanation: \"Sarung Banggi\" (One Evening) is a gentle and romantic song from Bicol that speaks of a pleasant encounter at night.\n9. C. They carry stories, values, and traditions of the Filipino people.\n   *Explanation: Folk songs serve as a living archive of Filipino culture, transmitting historical narratives, moral lessons, and cultural practices.\n10. B. The abundance of natural resources and simple living in the countryside.\n    *Explanation: \"Bahay Kubo\" paints a picture of a traditional Filipino home surrounded by various vegetables and fruits, symbolizing self-sufficiency and connection to nature.','[{\"question\":\"What is the primary characteristic of most Philippine folk songs?\",\"choices\":[\"They are often about love and courtship.\",\"They are usually religious in nature.\",\"They often tell stories of daily life, history, or cultural practices.\",\"They are exclusively sung in Spanish.\"],\"correct_index\":2,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Which of the following is a popular example of a children\'s folk song from the Philippines?\",\"choices\":[\"\\\"Noche Buena\\\"\",\"\\\"Bahay Kubo\\\"\",\"\\\"Leron Leron Sinta\\\"\",\"\\\"Magtanim Ay Di Biro\\\"\"],\"correct_index\":2,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"\\\"Leron Leron Sinta\\\" is a folk song that describes the hardships of:\",\"choices\":[\"Farmers harvesting rice.\",\"A person looking for a guava.\",\"Fishermen at sea.\",\"Children playing a game.\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"\\\"Magtanim Ay Di Biro\\\" is a folk song that highlights the challenges and nature of work for:\",\"choices\":[\"Weavers of traditional cloth.\",\"Farmers planting rice.\",\"Musicians performing in fiestas.\",\"Sailors navigating the seas.\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Folk songs in the Philippines often use simple melodies and are passed down through generations. This is an example of:\",\"choices\":[\"Classica