 their culture better.','[{\"question\":\"What is the primary characteristic of folk dances?\",\"choices\":[\"They are performed for professional entertainment.\",\"They are passed down from generation to generation within a community.\",\"They are characterized by complex choreography and strict technique.\",\"They are primarily developed by choreographers for stage performances.\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Which of the following is NOT typically a reason for folk dances to be performed?\",\"choices\":[\"To celebrate religious holidays and festivals.\",\"To commemorate historical events and achievements.\",\"To express personal emotions and introspection.\",\"To mark significant life events such as weddings and harvests.\"],\"correct_index\":2,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"In many folk dances, the costumes are significant because they often:\",\"choices\":[\"Are standardized across all regions and cultures.\",\"Reflect the available materials and climate of the region.\",\"Are inspired by modern fashion trends.\",\"Require expensive, imported fabrics.\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"What does the term \'regional variation\' mean in the context of folk dances?\",\"choices\":[\"All folk dances are identical worldwide.\",\"Folk dances adapt and change based on the specific locality.\",\"Folk dances are only performed in capital cities.\",\"Regional variations are discouraged in folk dancing.\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Many folk dances originated from:\",\"choices\":[\"Formal dance studios.\",\"The daily lives and work of people.\",\"Ballet schools.\",\"Modern hip-hop culture.\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Which of these is a common element found in many folk dances?\",\"choices\":[\"Highly technical ballet leaps and turns.\",\"Interpretive modern dance movements.\",\"Repetitive steps and formations that are easy to learn.\",\"Complex improvisation techniques.\"],\"correct_index\":2,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Folk dances contribute to cultural preservation by:\",\"choices\":[\"Replacing traditional customs with modern ones.\",\"Documenting and transmitting cultural heritage.\",\"Discouraging the use of traditional music.\",\"Focusing solely on athletic performance.\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"The music used in folk dances is often:\",\"choices\":[\"Composed by famous international musicians.\",\"Electronically produced and synthesized.\",\"Traditional and reflective of the local culture.\",\"Primarily classical orchestral music.\"],\"correct_index\":2,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"What is a \'formation\' in a folk dance?\",\"choices\":[\"A type of shoe worn by dancers.\",\"The arrangement of dancers on the floor.\",\"The specific steps performed by a single dancer.\",\"The costume worn by the lead dancer.\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Why is it important for young people to learn and participate in folk dances today?\",\"choices\":[\"To become professional dancers.\",\"To connect with their heritage and understand their culture better.\",\"To compete in international dance competitions.\",\"To learn complex, avant-garde dance styles.\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1}]',10,'gform',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'130DEYAbk8jbBtVbt7PBYWztQP4J1ROloNd2HW7mZzDY','https://docs.google.com/forms/d/130DEYAbk8jbBtVbt7PBYWztQP4J1ROloNd2HW7mZzDY/edit','https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeO6CgZqC6vmlujOrlURhXCUpE0_ECVPwIlocvwsI3iHQgwDg/viewform','Generated','2026-09-20 08:37:47','2026-09-20 08:37:47',NULL,NULL),(7,20,'ENG7',NULL,'quiz','Grade 7 English Term 1 Make-up Quiz','Catch-up session for missing q2','Dear Grade 7 students, you still have a missing requirement for English 7 Term 1. This short make-up quiz replaces your missed written and oral assessment. Please complete this task in the Student Portal. Keep in mind that you can answer this quiz only once. If you have any questions or need help, please ask your teacher. Good luck!',NULL,'[{\"question\":\"In the analogy \'author is to book as painter is to ____\', which word correctly completes the relationship?\",\"choices\":[\"canvas\",\"painting\",\"brush\",\"gallery\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Which of the following sentences is written in direct speech?\",\"choices\":[\"She said that she was happy.\",\"She said, \'I am happy.\'\",\"She told me to be happy.\",\"She asked if I was happy.\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"What is the voice of the verb in the sentence: \'The teacher graded the test papers.\'?\",\"choices\":[\"Active voice\",\"Passive voice\"],\"correct_index\":0,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Which of the following represents the correct passive voice form of \'The boy kicked the ball\'?\",\"choices\":[\"The ball is kicked by the boy.\",\"The ball was kicked by the boy.\",\"The ball had been kicked by the boy.\",\"The boy was kicking the ball.\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Which element of a short story refers to the time and place in which the story events happen?\",\"choices\":[\"Plot\",\"Conflict\",\"Setting\",\"Theme\"],\"correct_index\":2,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Which part of a story\'s plot introduces the characters, setting, and basic situation?\",\"choices\":[\"Climax\",\"Exposition\",\"Falling Action\",\"Resolution\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Which viewing genre aims primarily to provide factual information about real-life people, events, or issues?\",\"choices\":[\"Documentary\",\"Movie trailer\",\"Animated film\",\"Commercial\"],\"correct_index\":0,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Which reference material contains a collection of maps and geographical information?\",\"choices\":[\"Dictionary\",\"Thesaurus\",\"Atlas\",\"Encyclopedia\"],\"correct_index\":2,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"What type of literary conflict occurs when a character struggles against the rules or expectations of a group?\",\"choices\":[\"Man vs. Self\",\"Man vs. Man\",\"Man vs. Society\",\"Man vs. Nature\"],\"correct_index\":2,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"What is the main purpose of summarizing a text?\",\"choices\":[\"To copy the text word-for-word\",\"To state the main ideas in a shorter form\",\"To express personal opinions about the author\",\"To translate the text into another language\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1}]',10,'gform',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Sent','2026-09-20 18:51:38','2026-09-20 18:51:38','2026-09-20 18:51:38',NULL),(8,20,'AP8',NULL,'quiz','Araling Panlipunan 8 - Unang Markahan: Make-Up Quiz para sa Q3','Catch-up session for missing q3','Magandang araw. Nais kong ipabatid na mayroon ka pang hindi nairerehistrong marka para sa Written/Oral Works (Q3). Ang maikling make-up quiz na ito ay inihanda upang mapunan ang naturang kakulangan. Maaari mo itong sagutan sa iyong Student Portal. Tandaan na isang beses mo lamang ito pwedeng sagutan. Kung mayroon kang mga katanungan o nangangailangan ng tulong, huwag mag-atubiling magtanong sa iyong guro. Galingan mo!',NULL,'[{\"question\":\"Ano ang pinakamalaking kontinente sa daigdig sa sukat ng lupa at populasyon?\",\"choices\":[\"Asya\",\"Aprika\",\"Europa\",\"Hilagang Amerika\"],\"correct_index\":0,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Ano ang tawag sa supercontinent na sinasabing pinagmulan ng mga kasalukuyang kontinente ayon sa Teoryang Continental Drift?\",\"choices\":[\"Laurasia\",\"Pangaea\",\"Gondwanaland\",\"Tethys\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Aling sonang pangklima ang matatagpuan sa pagitan ng Kabilugang Arctic at Tropic of Cancer, kung saan karaniwang nararanasan ang apat na panahon?\",\"choices\":[\"Polar o Mataas na Latitud\",\"Tropikal o Mababang Latitud\",\"Gitnang Latitud o Katamtamang Klima\",\"Disyerto\"],\"correct_index\":2,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Sa anong yugto ng pag-unlad ng kultura nadiskubre ng mga sinaunang tao ang paggamit ng apoy at nagsimula silang mamuhay nang nomadiko?\",\"choices\":[\"Panahong Neolitiko\",\"Panahong Metal\",\"Panahong Paleolitiko\",\"Panahong Mesolitiko\"],\"correct_index\":2,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Ano ang pangunahing katangian ng Panahong Neolitiko na nagdulot ng malaking pagbabago sa pamumuhay ng mga sinaunang tao?\",\"choices\":[\"Pagsisimula ng agrikultura at permanenteng tirahan\",\"Paggamit ng mga kasangkapang gawa sa bakal\",\"Paglipat-lipat ng tirahan upang mangaso\",\"Pagpipinta sa mga dingding ng kuweba\"],\"correct_index\":0,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Anong kabihasnan ang itinuturing na \'Lunduyan ng Sibilisasyon\' (Cradle of Civilization) na matatagpuan sa pagitan ng mga ilog Tigris at Euphrates?\",\"choices\":[\"Ehipto\",\"Mesopotamia\",\"Indus\",\"Tsina\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Bakit tinaguriang \'Biyaya ng Nile\' (Gift of the Nile) ang sinaunang kabihasnan ng Ehipto?\",\"choices\":[\"Dahil ito lamang ang tanging anyong tubig sa buong kontinente\",\"Dahil ang taunang pagbaha nito ay nag-iiwan ng matabang lupa na angkop sa pagsasaka\",\"Dahil dito nagmula ang kanilang mga pangunahing kalaban\",\"Dahil ito ang pinagmulan ng kanilang mga ginto at pilak\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Alin sa mga sumusunod ang dalawang importanteng lungsod sa Kabihasnang Indus na nagpakita ng sopistikadong sistema ng pagpaplano ng lungsod (city planning)?\",\"choices\":[\"Ur at Babylon\",\"Memphis at Thebes\",\"Harappa at Mohenjo-Daro\",\"Xianyang at Luoyang\"],\"correct_index\":2,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Ano ang tawag sa kaisipang Tsino na nagpapaliwanag na ang pamumuno ng isang emperador ay may pahintulot o basbas mula sa kalangitan?\",\"choices\":[\"Mandate of Heaven\",\"Divine Right of Kings\",\"Legalismo\",\"Sinocentrism\"],\"correct_index\":0,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Aling sistema ng pagsulat ang ipinamana ng mga Sumerian sa kasaysayan ng daigdig?\",\"choices\":[\"Hieroglyphics\",\"Calligraphy\",\"Cuneiform\",\"Phoenician Alphabet\"],\"correct_index\":2,\"points\":1}]',10,'gform',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Sent','2026-09-20 19:12:26','2026-09-20 19:12:26','2026-09-20 19:12:26',NULL),(9,20,'ENG7',NULL,'quiz','Pros and Cons Quiz','10 items','# Quiz: Pros and Cons\n\nInstructions: Read each statement carefully and select the best answer.\n\n1. Which of the following is considered a \'Pro\' of using social media for students?\n   A. Easy access to educational resources\n   B. Increased risk of cyberbullying\n   C. Distraction from school work\n   D. Spread of misinformation\n\n2. Which of the following is considered a \'Con\' of distance learning?\n   A. Flexible study hours\n   B. Less physical interaction with peers\n   C. Reduced travel time\n   D. Personalized pacing\n\n3. A \'Pro\' is defined as:\n   A. An argument against an idea\n   B. A negative consequence\n   C. A positive aspect or advantage\n   D. A neutral summary\n\n4. A \'Con\' is defined as:\n   A. A reason in favor of something\n   B. A challenge, disadvantage, or negative aspect\n   C. A clear objective\n   D. A concluding statement\n\n5. Which is a \'Pro\' of participating in team sports?\n   A. High risk of physical injury\n   B. Development of teamwork and discipline\n   C. Time taken away from hobbies\n   D. Uniform costs\n\n6. Which is a \'Con\' of having a strictly regulated school uniform policy?\n   A. Promotes school spirit\n   B. Reduces social pressure based on clothing\n   C. Limits individual self-expression\n   D. Creates a professional atmosphere\n\n7. Identify the \'Pro\' of reading printed books over e-books:\n   A. Less eye strain and no battery required\n   B. Harder to carry around\n   C. Cannot adjust font size\n   D. Takes up physical shelf space\n\n8. Identify the \'Con\' of city living:\n   A. Access to many job opportunities\n   B. High levels of noise and pollution\n   C. Proximity to hospitals and malls\n   D. More entertainment options\n\n9. True or False: A pros and cons list is a tool used for decision-making.\n   A. True\n   B. False\n\n10. Which of these is a \'Con\' of staying up late to study?\n    A. Better understanding of the material\n    B. Improved sleep quality\n    C. Fatigue and difficulty concentrating the next day\n    D. More hours in the day','1. A - Pro is a benefit.\n2. B - Con is a disadvantage.\n3. C - Pro refers to advantages.\n4. B - Con refers to disadvantages.\n5. B - Teamwork is a positive outcome.\n6. C - Restriction of personal choice is often cited as a con.\n7. A - Physical books do not rely on screens.\n8. B - Noise and pollution are common urban challenges.\n9. A - It helps weigh options.\n10. C - Lack of sleep is a negative health/academic consequence.','[{\"question\":\"Which of the following is considered a \'Pro\' of using social media for students?\",\"choices\":[\"Easy access to educational resources\",\"Increased risk of cyberbullying\",\"Distraction from school work\",\"Spread of misinformation\"],\"correct_index\":0,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Which of the following is considered a \'Con\' of distance learning?\",\"choices\":[\"Flexible study hours\",\"Less physical interaction with peers\",\"Reduced travel time\",\"Personalized pacing\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"A \'Pro\' is defined as:\",\"choices\":[\"An argument against an idea\",\"A negative consequence\",\"A positive aspect or advantage\",\"A neutral summary\"],\"correct_index\":2,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"A \'Con\' is defined as:\",\"choices\":[\"A reason in favor of something\",\"A challenge, disadvantage, or negative aspect\",\"A clear objective\",\"A concluding statement\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Which is a \'Pro\' of participating in team sports?\",\"choices\":[\"High risk of physical injury\",\"Development of teamwork and discipline\",\"Time taken away from hobbies\",\"Uniform costs\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Which is a \'Con\' of having a strictly regulated school uniform policy?\",\"choices\":[\"Promotes school spirit\",\"Reduces social pressure based on clothing\",\"Limits individual self-expression\",\"Creates a professional atmosphere\"],\"correct_index\":2,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Identify the \'Pro\' of reading printed books over e-books:\",\"choices\":[\"Less eye strain and no battery required\",\"Harder to carry around\",\"Cannot adjust font size\",\"Takes up physical shelf space\"],\"correct_index\":0,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Identify the \'Con\' of city living:\",\"choices\":[\"Access to many job opportunities\",\"High levels of noise and pollution\",\"Proximity to hospitals and malls\",\"More entertainment options\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"True or False: A pros and cons list is a tool used for decision-making.\",\"choices\":[\"True\",\"False\"],\"correct_index\":0,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Which of these is a \'Con\' of staying up late to study?\",\"choices\":[\"Better understanding of the material\",\"Improved sleep quality\",\"Fatigue and difficulty concentrating the next day\",\"More hours in the day\"],\"correct_index\":2,\"points\":1}]',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Draft','2026-09-23 02:43:55','2026-09-23 02:43:55',NULL,NULL),(10,20,'ENG7',9,'quiz','Pros and Cons Quiz','10 items','# Quiz: Pros and Cons\n\nInstructions: Read each statement carefully and select the best answer.\n\n1. Which of the following is considered a \'Pro\' of using social media for students?\n   A. Easy access to educational resources\n   B. Increased risk of cyberbullying\n   C. Distraction from school work\n   D. Spread of misinformation\n\n2. Which of the following is considered a \'Con\' of distance learning?\n   A. Flexible study hours\n   B. Less physical interaction with peers\n   C. Reduced travel time\n   D. Personalized pacing\n\n3. A \'Pro\' is defined as:\n   A. An argument against an idea\n   B. A negative consequence\n   C. A positive aspect or advantage\n   D. A neutral summary\n\n4. A \'Con\' is defined as:\n   A. A reason in favor of something\n   B. A challenge, disadvantage, or negative aspect\n   C. A clear objective\n   D. A concluding statement\n\n5. Which is a \'Pro\' of participating in team sports?\n   A. High risk of physical injury\n   B. Development of teamwork and discipline\n   C. Time taken away from hobbies\n   D. Uniform costs\n\n6. Which is a \'Con\' of having a strictly regulated school uniform policy?\n   A. Promotes school spirit\n   B. Reduces social pressure based on clothing\n   C. Limits individual self-expression\n   D. Creates a professional atmosphere\n\n7. Identify the \'Pro\' of reading printed books over e-books:\n   A. Less eye strain and no battery required\n   B. Harder to carry around\n   C. Cannot adjust font size\n   D. Takes up physical shelf space\n\n8. Identify the \'Con\' of city living:\n   A. Access to many job opportunities\n   B. High levels of noise and pollution\n   C. Proximity to hospitals and malls\n   D. More entertainment options\n\n9. True or False: A pros and cons list is a tool used for decision-making.\n   A. True\n   B. False\n\n10. Which of these is a \'Con\' of staying up late to study?\n    A. Better understanding of the material\n    B. Improved sleep quality\n    C. Fatigue and difficulty concentrating the next day\n    D. More hours in the day','1. A - Pro is a benefit.\n2. B - Con is a disadvantage.\n3. C - Pro refers to advantages.\n4. B - Con refers to disadvantages.\n5. B - Teamwork is a positive outcome.\n6. C - Restriction of personal choice is often cited as a con.\n7. A - Physical books do not rely on screens.\n8. B - Noise and pollution are common urban challenges.\n9. A - It helps weigh options.\n10. C - Lack of sleep is a negative health/academic consequence.','[{\"question\":\"Which of the following is considered a \'Pro\' of using social media for students?\",\"choices\":[\"Easy access to educational resources\",\"Increased risk of cyberbullying\",\"Di