ocs.google.com/forms/d/18bsvgKDBfXxQyzvO6dzT_9S-Qcb-vMl-7ptctudDW2s/edit','https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdy0495i-TJmfi8oAbUXwUkCamEZAyKpx3Orit2-Bsk9gNURw/viewform','Sent','2026-09-23 02:58:53','2026-09-23 02:59:13','2026-09-23 02:59:13',NULL),(13,20,'MATH7',NULL,'quiz','Quiz: Identifying Rational Numbers','Identify rational numbers','# Mathematics 7 Quiz: Identifying Rational Numbers\n\nName: ______________________ Date: _________\n\nDirections: Choose the best answer for each question.\n\n1. Which of the following is a rational number?\nA. sqrt(2)\nB. 0.5\nC. pi\nD. non-terminating, non-repeating decimal\n\n2. Every integer is also a rational number.\nA. True\nB. False\n\n3. Which of the following can be expressed in the form p/q where p and q are integers and q is not equal to zero?\nA. 4/0\nB. 3/7\nC. sqrt(3)\nD. 0.1010010001...\n\n4. Is the number -5 a rational number?\nA. Yes\nB. No\n\n5. Which of these is NOT a rational number?\nA. 0.333...\nB. 22/7\nC. sqrt(5)\nD. 1/2\n\n6. A terminating decimal is always a rational number.\nA. True\nB. False\n\n7. What is the fractional form of 0.25?\nA. 1/2\nB. 1/4\nC. 2/5\nD. 1/5\n\n8. Repeating decimals like 0.666... are rational numbers.\nA. True\nB. False\n\n9. Which set of numbers contains only rational numbers?\nA. {1, 0, -2, 1/3}\nB. {sqrt(2), 3, 5, 1/4}\nC. {pi, 1, 0, 7}\nD. {sqrt(7), 1, 2, 4}\n\n10. The number 0 is a rational number.\nA. True\nB. False','1. B - Rational numbers can be written as simple fractions or decimals that terminate or repeat.\n2. A - Integers can be written as n/1.\n3. B - This is the formal definition of rational numbers.\n4. A - -5 can be written as -5/1.\n5. C - Square roots of non-perfect squares are irrational.\n6. A - Terminating decimals can be written as a/10, a/100, etc.\n7. B - 0.25 is equal to 25/100, which simplifies to 1/4.\n8. A - Repeating decimals can be expressed as fractions.\n9. A - All listed numbers are integers or simple fractions.\n10. A - 0 can be written as 0/1.','[{\"question\":\"Which of the following is a rational number?\",\"choices\":[\"sqrt(2)\",\"0.5\",\"pi\",\"non-terminating, non-repeating decimal\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Every integer is also a rational number.\",\"choices\":[\"True\",\"False\"],\"correct_index\":0,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Which of the following can be expressed in the form p\\/q where p and q are integers and q is not equal to zero?\",\"choices\":[\"4\\/0\",\"3\\/7\",\"sqrt(3)\",\"0.1010010001...\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Is the number -5 a rational number?\",\"choices\":[\"Yes\",\"No\"],\"correct_index\":0,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Which of these is NOT a rational number?\",\"choices\":[\"0.333...\",\"22\\/7\",\"sqrt(5)\",\"1\\/2\"],\"correct_index\":2,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"A terminating decimal is always a rational number.\",\"choices\":[\"True\",\"False\"],\"correct_index\":0,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"What is the fractional form of 0.25?\",\"choices\":[\"1\\/2\",\"1\\/4\",\"2\\/5\",\"1\\/5\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Repeating decimals like 0.666... are rational numbers.\",\"choices\":[\"True\",\"False\"],\"correct_index\":0,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"Which set of numbers contains only rational numbers?\",\"choices\":[\"{1, 0, -2, 1\\/3}\",\"{sqrt(2), 3, 5, 1\\/4}\",\"{pi, 1, 0, 7}\",\"{sqrt(7), 1, 2, 4}\"],\"correct_index\":0,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"The number 0 is a rational number.\",\"choices\":[\"True\",\"False\"],\"correct_index\":0,\"points\":1}]',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Draft','2026-09-23 06:47:42','2026-09-23 06:47:42',NULL,NULL),(14,20,'MATH7',13,'quiz','Quiz: Identifying Rational Numbers','Identify rational numbers','# Mathematics 7 Quiz: Identifying Rational Numbers\n\nName: ______________________ Date: _________\n\nDirections: Choose the best answer for each question.\n\n1. Which of the following is a rational number?\nA. sqrt(2)\nB. 0.5\nC. pi\