 Preference\n\n7. Chocolate ice cream is the best. This statement is an:\nA. Opinion\nB. Fact\nC. Observation\n\n8. The library opens at 8:00 AM. This is a:\nA. Feeling\nB. Fact\nC. Judgment\n\n9. Which word suggests an opinion is being expressed?\nA. Probably\nB. Number\nC. Date\n\n10. Facts are based on:\nA. Personal beliefs\nB. Reliable evidence\nC. Feelings\n\n11. Math class is boring. This is a:\nA. Fact\nB. Scientific measurement\nC. Opinion\n\n12. Which of these is a fact?\nA. The Earth orbits the Sun.\nB. Technology is beautiful.\nC. Blue pencils are better than red ones.\n\n13. Opinions cannot be proven true because they are:\nA. Personal\nB. Measured\nC. Recorded\n\n14. Which of the following is a fact about school life?\nA. The school has 20 classrooms.\nB. The school is the best place to be.\nC. School is too long.\n\n15. What kind of statement expresses a judgment or preference?\nA. Fact\nB. Opinion\nC. Scientific data\n\n16. Apples contain vitamin C. This is a:\nA. Fact\nB. Feeling\nC. Preference\n\n17. Which word indicates an opinion?\nA. Best\nB. 20\nC. 1998\n\n18. A statement that can be checked using records is a:\nA. Fact\nB. Opinion\nC. Preference\n\n19. Dogs are faster than turtles. This is a:\nA. Fact\nB. Opinion\nC. Personal belief\n\n20. If someone says \'in my opinion\', they are sharing:\nA. A proven fact\nB. A personal view\nC. A scientific record','1. B - Fact\n2. A - Opinion\n3. A - I think\n4. C - Fact\n5. B - Records or measurements\n6. A - Fact\n7. A - Opinion\n8. B - Fact\n9. A - Probably\n10. B - Reliable evidence\n11. C - Opinion\n12. A - The Earth orbits the Sun.\n13. A - Personal\n14. A - The school has 20 classrooms.\n15. B - Opinion\n16. A - Fact\n17. A - Best\n18. A - Fact\n19. A - Fact\n20. B - A personal view','[{\"question\":\"The Philippines has more than 7,000 islands. This sentence is:\",\"choices\":[\"Opinion\",\"Fact\",\"Both\"],\"correct_index\":1,\"points\":1},{\"question\":\"I believe math is easy. This sentence is: