nA. The school library is the best place to study.\nB. The library opens at exactly 8:00 AM.\nC. Students should spend more time reading.\nD. Reading is much more fun than playing games.\n\n2. Which of these is an opinion?\nA. The school year has four quarters.\nB. Our classroom has 30 desks.\nC. English is the most exciting subject to learn.\nD. The school bus arrives at 7:15 AM.\n\n3. Which phrase is a signal word commonly used for an opinion?\nA. It was recorded that\nB. In my opinion\nC. On the date of\nD. The measurement shows\n\n4. A statement that can be proven true or false by checking records is a:\nA. Judgment\nB. Fact\nC. Feeling\nD. Preference\n\n5. An opinion is best described as a statement that reflects:\nA. Scientific measurements\nB. Personal feelings or beliefs\nC. Documented historical dates\nD. Proven physical evidence\n\n6. Which of the following is an opinion?\nA. Apples contain Vitamin C.\nB. Blue pencils are better than red ones.\nC. The school has twenty classrooms.\nD. Water boils at 100 degrees Celsius.\n\n7. How can you verify if a statement is a fact?\nA. By asking for a friend\'s feeling\nB. By using a personal hunch\nC. By checking trusted records or measurements\nD. By seeing if it sounds beautiful\n\n8. Which sentence is a factual statement?\nA. Technology is the most fun way to learn.\nB. Dogs are generally faster than turtles.\nC. Science is harder than English.\nD. The school playground is the best in the city.\n\n9. Which word in a sentence often signals that it is an opinion?\nA. Probably\nB. Number\nC. Calendar\nD. Documented\n\n10. \"I believe that our school is the best.\" This is an example of an:\nA. Fact\nB. Opinion\nC. Measurement\nD. Official record','1. B - The library opens at exactly 8:00 AM.\n2. C - English is the most exciting subject to learn.\n3. B - In my opinion\n4. B - Fact\n5. B - Personal feelings or beliefs\n6. B - Blue pencils are better than red ones.\n7. C - By checking trusted records or measurements\n8.